,\\,14{x}^{2}+75x+80 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{14{x}^{2}+56x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,19x+80 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{19x+76}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $15{x}^{2}+14x+19\\,$ and $\\,14{x}^{2}+75x+80.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129117 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "dd4abd5d-2642-5f0d-af2f-5ed5c265526a" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bd97d62-c94c-52ff-9437-f46824a437a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550400} {:answer/id #uuid "a342682d-0b5e-57ab-a9de-6e55658f0cb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550790} {:answer/id #uuid "c6aa7498-c71d-56f0-81d7-3d56a57c52aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+2x+4\\,$ and $\\,4{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550904} {:answer/id #uuid "d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-4{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550939} {:answer/id #uuid "fbdd4a01-2551-59e8-a6f4-485a3a62c6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}+x-2\\,$ and $\\,2{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d37d0d7e-ef5b-5171-8f03-493fc100b9f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-4{x}^{2}-6x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550939} :answer-field/id #uuid "02161cfd-7963-5f8c-adc3-9f265f53ee14" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe67be82-4bb6-56a3-b9ff-5fcade759364" :question/math-academy-id "q-105592" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & 2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x+14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{2}+2x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8x+12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{2}-2x+4 \\\\  & 2x+3\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{4{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+2x+14\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4{x}^{2}+2x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,8x+14 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{8x+12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are \n\n$\\,$ $2{x}^{2}-2x+4\\,$ and $\\,-4{x}^{2}-6x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "237e2d45-91c4-5f95-88a4-a2f1d04dfafc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550450} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc6f7b6-8de8-58ea-beb7-3cbd3d284763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x+5-\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550507} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550641} {:answer/id #uuid "ca80d411-64cf-5d0d-b7d6-d10af63a7044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5-\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550914} {:answer/id #uuid "d2fad9ad-bc30-5420-a9c9-bc1e8dc40279" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x+5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e2bb91a-2c7f-5f78-b258-108514488718" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550641} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ba98643-df5a-5c60-a5a0-3f92f01fcd2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551150}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fd8cef0f-9754-53fc-971e-657a61c10786" :question/math-academy-id "q-37755" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6{x}^{2}-13x-5 \\\\  & -x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-6{x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,13{x}^{2}-21x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{13{x}^{2}-26x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5x+10 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{5x-10}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial $-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10$ by the linear binomial $-x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient $6{x}^{2}-13x-5,$ and\n\n- the remainder $20.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{-6{x}^{3}+25{x}^{2}-21x+10}{-x+2}=6{x}^{2}-13x-5+\\frac{20}{-x+2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551318 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "653168b4-614d-53c8-82ca-963c2033dbaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x+2\\,$ and $\\,-2x+4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550612} {:answer/id #uuid "830561b4-b28f-5d95-959b-58095c2da23b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-2\\,$ and $\\,2x+4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550699} {:answer/id #uuid "b24a463d-9be5-5bb5-bc05-5817742224c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3x-2\\,$ and $\\,2x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550853} {:answer/id #uuid "ef65b598-8ec9-5519-a1ab-5ea0b0d5f310" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x-1\\,$ and $\\,-4x-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551015} {:answer/id #uuid "f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f37a4a83-f662-5865-b736-284f5ac28587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551021} :answer-field/id #uuid "5193cf16-df21-588b-a599-9cd38ca21c4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551113}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a28bf299-6ff2-586b-9620-39977848687b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37964" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x-9\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-2 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x-9} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+2x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-2x-9 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,2x-4}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-2\\,$ and $\\,-2x-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129118 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "26c342f1-881b-5f3e-8c76-448eec165168" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Polynomial With Some Zero Coefficients by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0540677d-be4a-51e1-94f9-d3e8ea71916d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x-6\\,$ and $\\,6x+6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550383} {:answer/id #uuid "0d703983-3af1-569b-a566-2c0828d6c6e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+2\\,$ and $\\,6x-2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550404} {:answer/id #uuid "25c50f45-f213-5891-aa1b-f1cec1b70c2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2x-6\\,$ and $\\,2x+6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550460} {:answer/id #uuid "663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550621} {:answer/id #uuid "bd5e4bc8-abdd-5038-a814-a6f6cd9f14dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+1\\,$ and $\\,6x-1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "663209ff-7566-5af2-9a93-2c990afa622e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550621} :answer-field/id #uuid "31d78917-a444-511b-96e8-e5c516c9420d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551095}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8611bb27-3bf5-5d1d-beee-a73906924e0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-37988" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing expressions in the following polynomial division problem?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\boxed{} \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{\\boxed{}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x+6 \\\\  & x-1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{2}+0x-1} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{2}-6x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6x-6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $6x+6\\,$ and $\\,6x-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551274 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129120 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bdfd8fc-ce8d-5950-870d-c0570ef755bf" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Result of Dividing a Polynomial by a Linear Binomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6830041c-00d3-5d48-9372-4d91139f97be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+2+\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550626} {:answer/id #uuid "97cc9ca4-a5bf-5661-9880-56ef534212ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3-\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550754} {:answer/id #uuid "a3daa18e-f8f9-56bc-98a8-790e2c46a9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{2}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550794} {:answer/id #uuid "b62feedb-db0f-52e1-8d3c-c9470e9b162f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{17}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550865} {:answer/id #uuid "d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d133fb0d-db9f-5950-9d35-052a7275add0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550932} :answer-field/id #uuid "483aa0e1-ed0c-5589-8120-5205c6a8e4c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551110}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47e4cafc-245d-597a-859f-2f903cb45c89" :question/math-academy-id "q-38072" :question/problem "Consider the following polynomial division:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the above, $\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}=$" :question/worked-solution "$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4x+3 \\\\  & x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}+11x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}+8x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3x+11 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{3x+6}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given polynomial division, we deduce that dividing the polynomial ${x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11$ by the linear binomial $x+2$ gives\n\n- the quotient ${x}^{2}+4x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder $5.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+11x+11}{x+2}={x}^{2}+4x+3+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$"}]}
